---
title: The two feedback loops — CRAG and Self-RAG
---
stateDiagram-v2
    [*] --> Retrieve

    Retrieve --> GradeDocs: CRAG
    state GradeDocs {
        [*] --> Grading
        Grading --> [*]
    }

    GradeDocs --> Correct: any doc above threshold
    GradeDocs --> Ambiguous: mixed
    GradeDocs --> Incorrect: none pass

    Correct --> Refine: strip irrelevant sentences
    Ambiguous --> Both: internal + web
    Incorrect --> RewriteQ: discard all

    RewriteQ --> WebSearch
    WebSearch --> Retrieve: bounded retries

    Refine --> Generate
    Both --> Generate

    Generate --> VerifyCites: free, decisive
    VerifyCites --> Ungrounded: phantom marker or fake quote
    VerifyCites --> GradeAnswer: passes

    state GradeAnswer {
        [*] --> Groundedness : ISSUP
        Groundedness --> Utility : ISUSE
        Utility --> [*]
    }

    GradeAnswer --> Grounded: supported and useful
    GradeAnswer --> Ungrounded: unsupported claim or contradiction

    Ungrounded --> RewriteA: Self-RAG / RRR within max_retries
    RewriteA --> Retrieve
    Ungrounded --> Abstain: retries exhausted

    Grounded --> [*]
    Abstain --> [*]

    note right of Abstain
        An abstention is a success.
        Without one, the worst answers
        look exactly like the best.
    end note

    note right of VerifyCites
        Cheap check first: string matching
        catches fabricated attribution before
        any model call is spent on grading.
    end note
